## Getting started

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000).

## Controls

### Mouse / touch

| Input | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Drag | Spin the orb |
| Scroll / pinch | Zoom in & out |

### Keyboard

| Key | Action |
| --- | --- |
| `V` | Toggle voice |
| `R` | Reset the view |
| `+` / `−` | Zoom in / out |

## Arthemis CLI (vibe coding by terminal)

Same Arthemis pipeline without the browser, voice or TTS — what you type is exactly
what you would speak in the HUD:

```bash
npm run ares
```

```
> define o projeto atual como C:/meu-projeto
> cria um arquivo chamado src/app.ts com conteudo export const x = 1
> leia o arquivo src/app.ts
> troque export const por export let no arquivo src/app.ts
```

- With `KIWI_OLLAMA_API_KEY` set, the CLI uses **deepseek-v4-flash:cloud**;
  otherwise `KIWI_CLOUD_URL/KEY/MODEL` (OpenAI-compatible) or the local
  llama3.1 via Ollama.
- `/ajuda` for CLI commands, `/sair` to exit.
- Isolate its conversation history from the web app with
  `ARES_CONVERSATION_FILE=/tmp/conv.json npm run ares`.

## How it works

- **`lib/orbScene.ts`** — the Three.js scene: outer particle shell, synapse
  network core (particles.js-style), floating code-text sprites, dust particles
  and a neutral black-and-white post-processing stack.
- **`components/AresOrb.tsx`** — the HUD and glue between the scene, voice and
  the assistant.
- **`lib/agent/`** — the assistant core: built-in command engine (pt-BR),
  Ollama local + Ollama Cloud fallback, and tools for files, programs,
  WhatsApp, Instagram, other social networks, web search, and vibe coding
  (current-project, read_file, edit_file).
- **`scripts/ares-cli.ts`** — interactive terminal that drives the same
  `processCommand` pipeline.
- **`lib/voice.ts` + `app/api/tts/`** — natural neural voice (edge-tts)
  generated server-side, with browser TTS as fallback.

